# WHAT IS HIDDEN HERE, AND THE ONE RULE THAT DECIDES IT
#
# This repo is read and written by several Claude sessions and by the operator.
# Anything a future session cannot see, it will re-derive from scratch or, worse,
# contradict without knowing it did. So the default is VISIBLE, and the ignore
# list is short and has to justify itself.
#
# Exactly one thing is hidden on purpose: CREDENTIALS. A token pushed to GitHub
# is public permanently -- deletion does not un-publish it, because the object
# survives in the ref log and in anything that cloned or forked meanwhile. The
# Telethon *.session file is not a bot token, it is a live login to a PERSONAL
# Telegram account; committing one hands over the account.
#
# Everything else -- the ledger, the state, the reports, the absorbed findings --
# is EVIDENCE and belongs in the history where every brain can read it.

# ---- credentials: never, under any argument ------------------------------
*.key
*.token
*.env
.env
secrets/
credentials*
*_token*
*_password*
external/*.session
external/*.session-journal

# ---- machine noise -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.tmp
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
*.pyc.*

# ---- build artefact ------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerate with ./build_zip.sh. A committed zip goes stale the moment a module
# changes, and a packaged artifact that disagrees with its source is a failure
# mode this repo has already hit twice.
aurum_v2.zip

# ---- large binary market data -------------------------------------------
# Parquet bars are megabytes, regenerate exactly from the fetchers, and are not
# a claim anyone can be wrong about. Excluded for SIZE, not for secrecy: git is
# a poor object store for them and a bloated clone slows every session down.
# The derived reports and ledgers they produce are all committed.
*.parquet
data/**/*.parquet
data/**/*.csv.gz

# NOTE ON WHAT USED TO BE HERE.
# `state/`, `*.jsonl`, `acceptance_out/`, `backtest_out/`, `drift_out/` and
# `data/` were all ignored, under a comment reading "Local run artifacts --
# never evidence, never committed". That was flatly contradicted by run_desk.py,
# which prints "state/ledger.jsonl -- that file IS the forward evidence. Do not
# delete it." Both cannot be true. The ledger is the only record of what this
# desk actually predicted and what actually happened, it is the input to
# adapt.py's closed loop, and hiding it meant every new session started blind to
# every signal the desk had ever produced. They are now tracked.

# ---- the flows CACHE, and only the cache --------------------------------
# state/flows.json is a REFETCHABLE MIRROR of three public feeds (GLD tonnage,
# CFTC COT, Shanghai premium), not a record of anything this desk decided. It is
# excluded for one specific reason, and it is not size or secrecy:
#
# THIS CLONE CANNOT REACH THOSE FEEDS. The agent proxy answers every one of them
# with `403 Forbidden`, so a run here writes a file of nulls with an `errors`
# block and a FRESH `fetched_utc`. Committing that would push an all-null cache
# carrying today's timestamp on top of the one the VPS fetched successfully, and
# the desk would read it as a current, complete measurement of flows that are in
# fact simply unfetched. Absence wearing the timestamp of a measurement is
# exactly the failure the rest of this file exists to prevent.
#
# The flows that MATTER downstream — the prompt block the analyst was shown —
# travel in the ledger row's `brief_render`, which is committed. Nothing is lost.
state/flows.json

# ---- the desk state buffer -------------------------------------------------
# NOT a secret and NOT hidden evidence: the published copy lives on the
# `aurum-state` branch, one file per commit, every 15 minutes
#   git fetch origin aurum-state && git show origin/aurum-state:desk_state.json
# The local copy is a change-detection buffer only. It is ignored HERE because
# Update-AurumDesk.ps1 skips the auto-update whenever `git status --porcelain`
# is non-empty, so a tracked file rewritten every 15 minutes would silently
# stop the box from ever updating itself.
reports/desk_state.json
